      dealing: 'Tiles are mixed face down (darle agua). Each player in turn draws 10 tiles and places them on their rack hidden from others. The remaining 15 tiles stay face down and are not used during the round. Before the first deal, one player from each team draws a tile at random; the team whose tile has more spots plays first.',
    },
    turnFlow: "Tiles are played to form a line; touching ends of adjacent tiles must match. Doubles are played across the line at right angles; the line may turn corners. The first player may play any tile. Play continues counter-clockwise. On your turn you must add one tile to the line if you can; if you have no tile matching either open end you must pass. A round ends when one player plays their last tile (dominar or pegarse) or when the round is blocked (trancado): all four have tiles but none can play. When blocked, the player with fewest pips on remaining tiles wins the round. The winning team scores the total pips on the opponents' remaining tiles. The first team to 100 wins.",
