    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 10 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: As a team, score points by winning rounds (emptying your hand or having the lowest pip count when the round is blocked). The first team to reach a cumulative score of 100 or more wins the game.',
      "Turn-flow example: Tiles are played to form a line; touching ends of adjacent tiles must match. Doubles are played across the line at right angles; the line may turn corners. The first player may play any tile. Play continues counter-clockwise. On your turn you must add one tile to the line if you can; if you have no tile matching either open end you must pass. A round ends when one player plays their last tile (dominar or pegarse) or when the round is blocked (trancado): all four have tiles but none can play. When blocked, the player with fewest pips on remaining tiles wins the round. The winning team scores the total pips on the opponents' remaining tiles. The first team to 100 wins.",
      "Scoring example: Cumulative score per team. Winning team scores the total pips on the opponents' remaining tiles. First team to 100 or more wins the game. First team to reach a cumulative score of 100 or more points wins the game. Round winner is the first to empty hand or, when blocked, the player with fewest pips on remaining tiles..",
